{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q4492149","formula":"H₄O₆P₂","hill":"H4O6P2","elements":["H","O","P"],"composition":{"H":4.0,"O":6.0,"P":2.0},"names":{"en":"Hypophosphoric acid","ru":"Фосфорноватая кислота"},"descriptions":{"en":"Hypophosphoric acid is a mineral acid with the formula H4P2O6, with phosphorus in a formal oxidation state of +4. In the solid state it is present as the dihydrate, H4P2O6·2H2O. In hypophosphoric acid the phosphorus atoms are identical and joined directly with a P−P bond. Isohypophosphoric acid is a structural isomer of hypophosphoric acid in which one phosphorus has a hydrogen directedly bonded to it and that phosphorus atom is linked to the other one by an oxygen bridge to give a phosphorous acid/phosphoric acid mixed anhydride.","ru":"Фосфорноватая кислота — неорганическое соединение, четырёхосновная кислота с формулой H4P2O6, бесцветные кристаллы, растворяется в холодной воде с медленным разложением, образует кристаллогидраты."},"fame":12,"pubchemCid":24536,"mass":161.98,"charge":0,"smiles":"OP(=O)(O)P(=O)(O)O","inchikey":"TVZISJTYELEYPI-UHFFFAOYSA-N","iupac":"phosphonophosphonic acid","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"24536","atoms":12,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":1.096,"y":-0.069,"z":-0.054,"el":"P"},{"x":-1.101,"y":-0.072,"z":0.047,"el":"P"},{"x":1.719,"y":0.045,"z":1.44,"el":"O"},{"x":1.62,"y":1.313,"z":-0.721,"el":"O"},{"x":-1.729,"y":0.07,"z":-1.44,"el":"O"},{"x":-1.618,"y":1.297,"z":0.749,"el":"O"},{"x":1.595,"y":-1.283,"z":-0.789,"el":"O"},{"x":-1.582,"y":-1.301,"z":0.769,"el":"O"},{"x":2.686,"y":-0.074,"z":1.558,"el":"H"},{"x":2.57,"y":1.397,"z":-0.949,"el":"H"},{"x":-2.696,"y":-0.049,"z":-1.558,"el":"H"},{"x":-1.064,"y":2.103,"z":0.677,"el":"H"}],"bonds":[[0,1,1],[0,2,1],[0,3,1],[0,6,2],[1,4,1],[1,5,1],[1,7,2],[